<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Virata</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Virata is a king of the Matsya kingdom in the Indian epic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a>. The five Pandava brothers and their wife <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/draupadi">Draupadi</a> spend the thirteenth year of their exile in disguise at his court, and his daughter Uttara marries <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arjuna">Arjuna</a>'s son Abhimanyu. Virata fights for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandavas">Pandavas</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurukshetra">Kurukshetra</a> war and is killed by Drona. Tradition linked his name to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bairat">Viratanagara</a>, modern Bairat.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/virata.jpg" alt="Virata" width="320" height="476" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ravi Varma Press · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Virata%27s_Palace.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
